{"abstract":"This paper explores how the smartphone's form could be designed to help users establish more intentional usage patterns. A research through design approach that was based in design fiction principles resulted in three design proposals and scenarios, the Planning Phone, the Parasite Phone, and the Placeful Phone. These were evaluated in a focus group and analysed to develop a deeper understanding of how design researchers and developers can use ideas of authorship, barriers and norms to support intentional smartphone use.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Stepanovic, Mila","Boer, Laurens","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382596"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Polytechnic University of Milan"],"keyword":["Smartphone Intentional use Design Research Interaction Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconfiguring the smartphone to support intentional use","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114576/nordichi22_37.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382596","identifier":[{"id":"85140887109","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-598d5d49-7caf-4e8f-a0df-31b06095f2b0"],"keyword":["Smartphone, Intentional use, Design Research, Interaction Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-525DC3A9A4B88F765F842A0ECFFE574F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/87114576/nordichi22_37.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"polytechnic university of milan","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Polytechnic University of Milan","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Design Research Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mila","key":"stepanovicpau","last":"Stepanovic","name":"Stepanovic, Mila","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3546675","isbn":["9781450396998"],"pages":"1","place":"Aarhus, Denmark","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140887109"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-598d5d49-7caf-4e8f-a0df-31b06095f2b0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reconfiguring the Smartphone to Support Intentional Use","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382596","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Turning on a water tap in one’s home is an easy, simple and typically solitary interaction that masks the huge amounts of resources and efforts behind the collection, processing, and delivery of fresh water. There are many design and design research examples that aim to raise environmental awareness by draw- ing attention to consumption of domestic utilities. However, less common are designs that aim to provoke reflection on sustainable behaviors through an effort- ful and shared interaction. In this paper we present ‘Touchy Tap’ - a multi-touch kitchen faucet prototype in the form of a dynamically illuminated 2-meter wavy tube that requires control by two people. A slow interaction was designed with the intention to evoke reflections in use on issues related to water consumption. A preliminary evaluation indicates the potential of this ‘slow technology’ ap- proach to highlight water consumption issues, even though the ambiguity of such an unconventional interface may negatively impact on overall user experiences.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nakamura, Nanami","Mitchell, Robb","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382046"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Environmental awareness","Interactive design","Slow Technology","Sustainable behavior","Water consumption"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"touchy tap a slow technology for shared reflections on water consumption","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92561574/54_touchytapaslowtechnology.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382046","ids":["itu-34eabba0-3ae4-430c-b5cd-f003f77cc3cc"],"keyword":["Environmental Awareness","Interactive Design","Slow Technology","Sustainable Behavior","Water Consumption"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DC6AF459BB7341A73D89505FF667C668"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92561574/54_touchytapaslowtechnology.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanami","key":"nakamurapau","last":"Nakamura","name":"Nakamura, Nanami","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robb","key":"mitchellpau","last":"Mitchell","name":"Mitchell, Robb","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"EAI International Conference on ArtsIT, Interactivity &amp; Game Creation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-34eabba0-3ae4-430c-b5cd-f003f77cc3cc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Touchy Tap: a Slow Technology for Shared Reflections on Water Consumption","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382046","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Historically, blood glucose monitoring (BGM) device design has focused on the physiological aspects of diabetes, with less consideration for the psychological aspects of relating the measurement to one's experienced symptoms. In this pictorial, we explore how the subjective experience of blood glucose monitoring can be supported. We developed the BGM diary, a training system for existing BGM devices. The BGM diary involves a practice of guessing and measuring of blood glucose, followed by an annotation of felt symptoms to facilitate learning about experiences and symptoms. We unpack how blood glucose work could involve persons with diabetes in other ways in their care program through an elaboration on the design aspects of the BGM diary and reflections with a diabetes nurse.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Heiselberg, Kasper","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S02-082.86-029310"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","end":"2022-06-17","place":"Virtual, Online, au","start":"2022-06-13","title":"2022 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference: Digital Wellbeing, DIS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Blood Glucose Monitoring","Diabetes","Self Management Technology","Subjective Experiences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bgm diary supporting subjective experience in blood glucose management training","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86846363/BGM_DIS2022_Camera_Ready_V3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-082.86-029310","identifier":[{"id":"85133577423","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e5a06140-1e79-4b08-b180-5f925adc4210","itu-818b9c3c-fa25-4f37-a32e-47c95e9fc110"],"keyword":["Diabetes","blood glucose monitoring","self-management technology","subjective experiences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-41B645FCBB0725E01947A029D74B58DD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86846363/BGM_DIS2022_Camera_Ready_V3.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Socio-Technical Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"heiselbergpau","last":"Heiselberg","locid":"80e19241-18bc-4749-a81a-5129ce88c91f","name":"Heiselberg, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3532106.3533475","isbn":["9781450393591"],"pages":"1849-1862","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"DIS 2022 - Proceedings of the 2022 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference: Digital Wellbeing","status":"p","title":"DIS '22 Companion: Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133577423"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e5a06140-1e79-4b08-b180-5f925adc4210","itu-818b9c3c-fa25-4f37-a32e-47c95e9fc110"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BGM Diary : Supporting Subjective Experience in Blood Glucose Management Training","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.86-029310","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Creative confidence is a concept that has been popularly linked to design thinking in more generalist interaction design education. Based on an analysis of creative confidence, however, we propose that Speculative and Critical Design practices (SCD) can be a better perspective for developing creative confidence in aspiring designers. We present how we have taught two subsequent SCD courses as part of a short 2-year generalist interaction design master’s programme. Based on the outcome of selected student projects, course evaluations, and personal reflections, we articulate the promises and pitfalls of using SCD to foster creative confidence.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Jenkins, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384294"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creative Confidence","Creative Self Beliefs","Creative Self Image","Design","Education","Interaction design","Speculative and Critical Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fostering creative confidence with scd in interaction design education","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.55612/s-5002-051-012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384294","identifier":[{"id":"85129412031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ce8c63cd-76ac-4a45-b35b-dcc9fe8b6bbb"],"keyword":["Creative Confidence","Creative Self-Beliefs","Creative Self-Image","Design","Education","Interaction Design","Speculative and Critical Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-D927E74668E1F865180122F0E5844270"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90369441/51_12.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.55612/s-5002-051-012","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.55612/s-5002-051-012","issn":["18269745","22832998"],"issn_org":["18269745"],"issue":"51","journal":"Interaction Design and Architecture","pages":"270-302","paperid":"12","publisher":"Interaction Design and Architecture(s)","status":"p","title":"Interaction Design and Architecture","title_org":"Interaction Design & Architecture(s)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129412031"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ce8c63cd-76ac-4a45-b35b-dcc9fe8b6bbb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fostering Creative Confidence with SCD in Interaction Design Education","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384294","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Physical computing concerns the design of systems that can sense and respond to the world around them, which is why it is often used in interaction design projects in educational settings. However, students who encounter physical computing for the first time are typically not aware of the form factors and the potential for interaction of the various sensing and actuating possibilities. To complement existing touchpoints that these students have with physical computing, we present electronic smörgåsbords: boards that display collections of physical computing components that are available inhouse in an organised and interactive way to support the initiation of interaction design projects. The development of the boards allowed us to articulate four principles for their design, which are intended to inspire the development of future educational material.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey","Cahill, Ben","Trier, Steffen Hviid"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383786"],"event":{"acronym":"TEI","title":"International Conference on Tangible, Embedded and Embodied Interactions"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design principles","Educational tools","Electronic smörgåsbords","Interaction design","Physical computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"smörgåsbords for physical computing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85746516/TEI2021_Boards_Camera_Ready2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383786","identifier":[{"id":"85102044804","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ada89c3c-1df8-4bd6-95a4-7a9ceedc767d"],"keyword":["Design principles","Educational tools","Electronic smörgåsbords","Interaction design","Physical computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B4199A54CD85746CB99EAE0C2E91A556"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85746516/TEI2021_Boards_Camera_Ready2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen Hviid","key":"trierpau","last":"Trier","name":"Trier, Steffen Hviid","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3430524.3446077","eisbn":["9781450382137/21/02."],"pages":"1","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"TEI '21: Fifteenth International Conference on Tangible, Embedded, and Embodied Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102044804"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ada89c3c-1df8-4bd6-95a4-7a9ceedc767d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Smörgåsbords for Physical Computing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383786","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Since the advent of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Machine Learning (ML), researchers have asked how intelligent computing systems could interact with and relate to their users and their surroundings, leading to debates around issues of biased AI systems, ML black-box, user trust, user's perception of control over the system, and system's transparency, to name a few. All of these issues are related to how humans interact with AI or ML systems, through an interface which uses different interaction modalities. Prior studies address these issues from a variety of perspectives, spanning from understanding and framing the problems through ethics and Science and Technology Studies (STS) perspectives to finding effective technical solutions to the problems. But what is shared among almost all those efforts is an assumption that if systems can explain the how and why of their predictions, people will have a better perception of control and therefore will trust such systems more, and even can correct their shortcomings. This research field has been called Explainable AI (XAI). In this studio, we take stock on prior efforts in this area; however, we focus on using Tangible and Embodied Interaction (TEI) as an interaction modality for understanding ML. We note that the affordances of physical forms and their behaviors potentially can not only contribute to the explainability of ML systems, but also can contribute to an open environment for criticism. This studio seeks to both critique explainable ML terminology and to map the opportunities that TEI can offer to the HCI for designing more sustainable, graspable and just intelligent systems.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ghajargar, Maliheh","Bardzell, Jeffrey","Renner, Alison Smith","Krogh, Peter Gall","Höök, Kristina","Cuartielles, David","Boer, Laurens","Wiberg, Mikael"],"cuid":["S02-093.25-022936"],"event":{"acronym":"TEI","end":"2021-02-17","place":"Virtual, Online, at","start":"2021-02-14","title":"15th International Conference on Tangible, Embedded, and Embodied Interaction, TEI 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Decisive Analytics Corporation","Malmö University","Pennsylvania State University","Pensylvania State University","Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Artificial intelligence","Explainable AI","Interaction design","Machine learning","TEI","Tangible Embodied Interaction","XAI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from explainable ai to graspable ai","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3430524.3442704","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-093.25-022936","identifier":[{"id":"85102059863","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8d01b573-3e91-4b34-9991-82fdea1572d2","itu-88c1c61c-77db-4af8-84a0-1849c3c7660a"],"keyword":["Artificial Intelligence","Explainable AI","Interaction Design","Machine Learning","TEI","Tangible Embodied Interaction","XAI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2D3C8E56AE951E6F6D84A1B38312F74D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85765499/GraspableAI_Description.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3430524.3442704","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, E