ion for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"TEI' 2021 - Proceedings of the 15th International Conference on Tangible, Embedded, and Embodied Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102059863"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8d01b573-3e91-4b34-9991-82fdea1572d2","itu-88c1c61c-77db-4af8-84a0-1849c3c7660a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"From \"Explainable AI\" to \"Graspable AI\"","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-093.25-022936","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The emerging science of the “gut-brain axis” has been used as the basis for self-tracking technologies assuming that this connection can be used productively for better regulating mood, supporting digestive health, and avoiding disease. Taking this emerging science as a source of design inspiration, this paper presents a design research process to uncover opportunities for novel interaction design and generate alternative approaches to self-tracking. We explored how this emerging scientific knowledge might be experienced and used and what these design spaces might look like through designing a self-tracking probe and asking science communicators working with the gut-brain axis to live with that probe. Their reactions led to a set of exploratory interaction design briefs and a more refined research product that collectively articulate how design can engage with emerging science to inspire a new perspective on self-tracking practices—one of cultivation rather than control.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Boer, Laurens","Homewood, Sarah","Almeida, Teresa","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383239"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","title":"Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Umeå University"],"keyword":["Design Research Process","Emerging Science","Gut brain axis","Interaction design","Self tracking Technologies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing with emerging science developing an alternative frame for self tracking","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85541703/Designing_with_Emerging_Science.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383239","identifier":[{"id":"85101780422","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-861bac2d-ff73-4c06-922a-f6599c7bf05d"],"keyword":["Design Research Process","Emerging Science","Gut-Brain Axis","Interaction Design","Self-Tracking Technologies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A47ECAFAD82051D65E7ECCC6343D4ADB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85541703/Designing_with_Emerging_Science.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"almeidapau","last":"Almeida","name":"Almeida, Teresa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3441000.3441020","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"32nd Australian Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101780422"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-861bac2d-ff73-4c06-922a-f6599c7bf05d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing with Emerging Science : Developing an Alternative Frame for Self-Tracking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383239","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"This one-day workshop will bring together researchers working with biodata and design for discussing and reflecting upon how design and HCI operate with the body and its data. The main workshop objective will be to identify core challenges and opportunities in this domain. We intend to cohere the projects of the workshop participants into a set of artifacts, images, and theory to create an annotated portfolio that represents the state-of-the art in designing with biodata in HCI. The workshop will be structured around four themes relating to the use and contexts of working with biodata: 1. Making sense of biodata by taking into account a holistic perspective of body, mind and emotions, as exemplified through soma design methods in HCI, for example; 2. Feminist perspectives of biodata that take into account bodily transitions, pluralities of bodies and temporalities of bodies; 3. Non-anthropocentric perspectives of working with and making sense of biodata, to also account for microorganisms and other material agencies in our bodies; and 4. Emerging domains, contexts, and practices around the use of biodata, such as health, affective, and performance contexts. The significance of the workshop is twofold: One, we will produce a group of researchers and practitioners that are working with biodata, aiming to unpack, discuss and respond to critical issues around designing with and for it. Two, we will create an annotated portfolio that can travel on its own as documentation and vision for future biodata-based design practices.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Jenkins, Tom","Boer, Laurens","Homewood, Sarah","Howell, Noura","Sanches, Pedro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382301"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","North Carolina State University"],"keyword":["Biodata","Biosensing","Interaction design","Materials"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenges and opportunities for designing with biodata as material","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85482286/NordiCHI_Workshop_Submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382301","identifier":[{"id":"85095815573","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-45a468bf-42d2-406a-85c7-c7921666f024"],"keyword":["biodata","biosensing","interaction design","materials"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F65B3BA29D24717960703EC533733EA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85482286/NordiCHI_Workshop_Submission.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"north carolina state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"North Carolina State University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Noura","key":"howellpau","last":"Howell","name":"Howell, Noura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"sanchespau","last":"Sanches","name":"Sanches, Pedro","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3419249.3420063","eisbn":["9781450375795"],"pages":"1-3","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '20: Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123042129"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-45a468bf-42d2-406a-85c7-c7921666f024"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Challenges and Opportunities for Designing with Biodata as Material","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382301","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"As self-tracking practices continue to proliferate, there has been a call for a consideration of how the design of these devices influence the users experience of themselves and their bodies beyond utility, efficacy and accuracy. The research product Ovum was designed to facilitate a DIY, shared, domestic experience, rather than an expert-led, individual, clinical experience of fertility tracking. Ovum uses the method of saliva sampling to determine ovulation. This paper unpacks the findings from a three-month long deployment of Ovum with seven couples trying to conceive. Besides an evaluation of the device in terms of the three experiential qualities aimed for in the design process, we report on the consequences of executing a design deployment that resembles a clinical trial. We contribute our experience in order to develop an understanding of how designing for the body places interaction designers in novel and complex situations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Homewood, Sarah","Boer, Laurens","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384362"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fertility","Menstrual Cycles","Ovulation","Research through Design","Self tracking","Women s health"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designers in white coats deploying ovum a fertility tracking device","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85072234/post_camera_ready_source_Ovum_Camera_Ready_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384362","identifier":[{"id":"85090495367","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d27df4f4-63e2-42e0-a63c-bd3bf82dd2ad"],"keyword":["Fertility","Menstrual Cycles","Ovulation;","Research through Design","Self-Tracking","Women’s Health"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E4F38110F34A926852B086AD2C4B7DE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85072234/post_camera_ready_source_Ovum_Camera_Ready_4.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3313831.3376528","eisbn":["9781450367080/20/04"],"place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2020 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090495367"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d27df4f4-63e2-42e0-a63c-bd3bf82dd2ad"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designers in White Coats: Deploying Ovum, a Fertility Tracking Device","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384362","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Ethnographic Experiential Futures (EXF) is an approach to foresight that aims to increase the accessibility, variety and depth of images of the future for design. In this paper, we present a EXF-based case study imagining the future supermarket. Rooted in already-existing images of future supermarkets, we propose that the future supermarket experience is autonomous, efficient, informed, local and personal. Based on the idea of four \"generic futures\" we illustrate each of these categories with a set of scenarios in a variety of experiential forms. These were exhibited first in an open exhibition and second in a closed exhibition for experts. To close, we offer reflections on the use of Ethnographic Experiential Futures in the form of a set of questions to inspire future research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Boer, Laurens","Busboom, Juliane Brigitta","Simonsen, Ivar Østby"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382726"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design research","Ethnographic Experiential Futures","Exhibition","Futures","Interaction design","Scenarios"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the future supermarket a case study of ethnographic experiential futures","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85479292/supermarket_preprint.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382726","identifier":[{"id":"85095849994","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-61083787-8580-43d8-98e8-17fccdce9ba9"],"keyword":["Design Research.","Ethnographic Experiential Futures","Exhibition","Futures","Interaction Design","Scenarios"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9CC895EA65E9E2DE4310443BAC39728E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85479292/supermarket_preprint.docx","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Juliane Brigitta","key":"busboompau","last":"Busboom","name":"Busboom, Juliane Brigitta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivar Østby","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","name":"Simonsen, Ivar Østby","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3419249.3420130","eisbn":["9781450375795"],"pages":"1-13","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '20: Shaping Experiences, Shaping Society"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123042554"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-61083787-8580-43d8-98e8-17fccdce9ba9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Future Supermarket : A Case Study of Ethnographic Experiential Futures","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382726","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Contemporary self-tracking devices take forms that reflect particular cultures of self-tracking that emphasize clinical perspectives and numerical precision. In this pictorial, we explore alternative forms to speculate on other possible self-tracking cultures. We present how we involved experts on the relationship between the gut and the brain to inspire a design brief for an alternative gut tracking device. This led to the design of Loupe and Lightbox, which together operate to externalize gut biota for closer examination, aesthetic appreciation, and reflection on the self. The device represents an example of self-tracking as cultivation—building a longer-term relationship with the self as something to be nurtured, tended to, and cared about.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey","Jenkins, Tom","Homewood, Sarah","Almeida, Teresa","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383724"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gut brain axis","Gut health","Probes","Research through Design","Self Tracking Devices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gut tracking as cultivation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85241372/dispx1114_boerA.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383724","identifier":[{"id":"85090499959","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a8d3f4a1-9c48-4e63-9891-d09e6ea07413"],"keyword":["Gut-Brain Axis","Gut-Health","Probes","Research through design","Self-Tracking Devices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E61DD573834D92716D23CBAFE85C1FE0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85241372/dispx1114_boerA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"almeidapau","last":"Almeida","name":"Almeida, Teresa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3357236.3395588","pages":"561-574","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DIS '20: Proceedings of the 2020 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090499959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a8d3f4a1-9c48-4e63-9891-d09e6ea07413"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gut-Tracking as Cultivation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383724","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Genetic factors partly determine the risk for premature myocardial infarction (MI). Objectives: We report the identification of a novel rare genetic variant in a kindred with an autosomal dominant trait for premature MI and atherosclerosis and explored the association of a common nonsynonymous variant in the same gene with the risk of ischemic heart disease (IHD) in a population-based study. Methods: Next-generation sequencing was performed in a small pedigree with premature MI or subclinical atherosclerosis. A common variant, rs8141797 A>G (p.Asn466Ser), in sushi domain–containing protein 2 (SUSD2) was studied in the prospective Copenhagen General Population Studies (N = 105,408) for association with IHD. Results: A novel heterozygous nonsense mutation in SUSD2 (c.G583T; p.Glu195Ter) was associated with the disease phenotype in the pedigree. SUSD2 protein was expressed in aortic specimens in the subendothelial cell layer and around the vasa vasorum. Furthermore, the minor G-allele of rs8141797 was associated with per allele higher levels of SUSD2 mRNA expression in the heart and vasculature. In the Copenhagen General Population Study, hazard ratios for IHD were 0.92 (95% CI: 0.87–0.97) in AG heterozygotes and 0.86 (0.62–1.19) in GG homozygotes vs noncarrriers (P-trend =.002). Finally, in meta-analysis including 73,983 IHD cases and 215,730 controls, the odds ratio for IHD per G-allele vs A-allele was 0.93 (0.90–0.96) (P = 4.6 × 10−7). Conclusions: The identification of a truncating mutation in SUSD2, which was associated with premature MI and subclinical atherosclerosis, combined with the finding that a common missense variant in SUSD2 was strongly associated with a lower risk of IHD, suggest that SUSD2 may alter the risk of atherosclerosis.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bruikman, Caroline S.","Dalila, Nawar","van Capelleveen, Julian C.","Kroon, Jeffrey","Peter, Jorge","Havik, Stefan R.","Willems, Martine","Huisman, Laurens C.","de Boer, Onno J.","Hovingh, G. Kees","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Dallinga-Thie, Geesje M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-459335"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["Academic Medical Centre","All Global Affiliations","Flevoziekenhuis Almere"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Genetics","Human","Myocardial Infarction","Premature atherosclerosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic variants in i susd000000000002 i are associated with the risk of ischemic heart disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-459335","identifier":[{"id":"32620384","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85087343456","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6e4b6ac6-1d11-4309-817f-857078932b4a"],"keyword":["Epidemiology","Genetics","Human","Myocardial infarction","Premature atherosclerosis","SUSD2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-936D6165F451714DBAFED80EC73D5F9B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"academic medical centre","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Academic Medical Centre","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"flevoziekenhuis almere","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Flevoziekenhuis Almere","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline S.","key":"bruikmanpau","last":"Bruikman","name":"Bruikman, Caroline S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nawar","key":"dalilapau","last":"Dalila","name":"Dalila, Nawar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Julian C.","key":"vancapelleveenpau","last":"van Capelleveen","name":"van Capelleveen, Julian C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeffrey","key":"kroonpau","last":"Kroon","name":"Kroon, Jeffrey","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jorge","key":"peterpau","last":"Peter","name":"Peter, Jorge","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stefan R.","key":"havikpau","last":"Havik","name":"Havik, Stefan R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Martine","key":"willemspau","last":"Willems","name":"Willems, Martine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Laurens C.","key":"huismanpau","last":"Huisman","name":"Huisman, Laurens C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Onno J.","key":"deboerpau","last":"de Boer","name":"de Boer, Onno J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"G. Kees","key":"hovinghpau","last":"Hovingh","name":"Hovingh, G. Kees","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne","key":"tybjaerghansenpau","last":"Tybjaerg-Hansen","locid":"452a492e-c869-41e5-b60e-1d2a542287cf","name":"Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","name_org":"Tybjaerg-Hansen, Anne","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Geesje M.","key":"dallingathiepau","last":"Dallinga-Thie","name":"Dallinga-Thie, Geesje M.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32620384"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacl.2020.05.100","issn":["19332874"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Clinical Lipidology","pages":"470-481","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Lipidology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087343456"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6e4b6ac6-1d11-4309-817f-857078932b4a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genetic variants in <i>SUSD2</i> are associated with the risk of ischemic heart disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-459335","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Medical devices are moving out of the clinic and into the home. The design of these devices shapes our experience of interacting with our bodies. We attend to ovulation tracking devices that aid conception. We present Ovum; a research product that will be deployed in a long-term, qualitative study with couples trying to conceive. The contributions of this pictorial are the framing of the design space around at-home ovulation tracking devices and the presentation of our approach to this design space through working with oppositional experiential qualities by designing for fertility tracking as a shared, domestic and do-it-yourself experience.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Homewood, Sarah","Bewley, Harvey","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382842"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fertility Tracking","Home Medical Devices","Ovulation Monitoring","Qualitative study","User Centered Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ovum designing for fertility tracking as a shared and domestic experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679270/Ovum_pictorial.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382842","identifier":[{"id":"85070585819","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69335158-fa16-42a2-a9cc-963bd80e3b49"],"keyword":["Fertility Tracking","Home Medical Devices","Ovulation Monitoring","Qualitative Study","User-Centered Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE98EED9E4FB4C349C8B108CBAB7BAD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679270/Ovum_pictorial.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3322276.3323692","eisbn":["9781450358507"],"pages":"553-565","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DIS '19 Proceedings of the 2019 on Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070585819"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69335158-fa16-42a2-a9cc-963bd80e3b49"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ovum: Designing for Fertility Tracking as a Shared and Domestic Experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382842","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This short paper offers a rationale and manifesto for a design-led research project called careful devices—domestic healthcare technologies that seek to bridge the gap between the lived experience of a person and the abstracted medical knowledge of a health practitioner. The rationale places careful devices at the intersection of contemporary trends in self-tracking and health care technology, and explains how and why this intersection is relevant for future interaction design. This is followed by a manifesto that articulates design goals for producing devices linking these trends, creating a space for interaction design research. We end with a discussion of Ovum, an example of a careful fertility tracking device.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Homewood, Sarah","Almeida, Teresa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381296"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CARE","Futures","Health","Interaction","Research through Design","Speculation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"careful devices a design manifesto for humane domestic healthcare technology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84703912/HttF_Careful_Devices_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381296","identifier":[{"id":"85076816462","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-02cc008c-840a-417f-9f81-b42ee744c0d7"],"keyword":["care","futures","health","interaction","research through design","speculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B69895ECD2235DF0BDA927567363863"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84703912/HttF_Careful_Devices_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Teresa","key":"almeidapau","last":"Almeida","name":"Almeida, Teresa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3363384.3363474","eisbn":["9781450372039"],"place":"Nottingham, United Kingdom","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Halfway to the Future Symposium 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076816462"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-02cc008c-840a-417f-9f81-b42ee744c0d7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Careful Devices : A design manifesto for humane domestic healthcare technology","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381296","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The increasing excessive, automated or unaware use of smartphones calls for a better understanding and design of ‘mindful’ interactions with this device. In this 2-week study with 11 participants we focus on the influence of the operating system’s interface in inviting for ‘mindful’ or ‘mindless’ interactions. Patterns of smartphone use were studied with a standard interface for the first week, and a reconfigured interface for the second week - the reconfigured interface being designed for more intentional use. Based on the study results we formulate a set of 5 design research themes for mindful interaction, and illustrate them in a conceptual proposal.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kühn, Lena","Hermann, Charlotte","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381451"],"event":{"acronym":"SHI","title":"Scandinavian Conference on Health Informatics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Interaction design","Mindful Interaction","Mobile technology","User Friendliness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design research themes for mindful interaction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84678766/ecp19161005.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381451","ids":["itu-0ca36e3f-44d6-4a63-8629-6e8510349c87"],"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Interaction Design","Mindful Interaction","Mobile Technology","User Friendliness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F56854384E3884B53B6009CA41A14F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ep.liu.se/ecp/161/005/ecp19161005.pdf","version":"