{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Bewley, Harvey","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381450"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how was it made social robotic donuts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84457593/HWIM_MayJune19_Review.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381450","identifier":[{"id":"85059554606","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0c78f463-eba9-4164-b5b9-1e2c882c39dc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-5-F11E257D9A2B9C9ABF7F6E3D13270A16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84457593/HWIM_MayJune19_Review.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3320503","issn":["10725520","15583449"],"issn_org":["10725520"],"issue":"3","journal":"interactions","pages":"14-15","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"interactions","volume":"26"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0c78f463-eba9-4164-b5b9-1e2c882c39dc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Was it Made? Social Robotic Donuts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381450","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In order to broaden the design space for social robot design, we created two air-actuated donutshaped social robots: a small uniform silicone version and a more organic latex version. Our intent was to move away from typical human or animal form mimicry, focusing instead on elastic expression, ambiguous form, and playful behaviors. Early studies show the robots provoking curious relationships with these contestational objects, inviting new forms of intriguing communication and interaction.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381603"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Air actuated","Ambiguous form","Elastic expression","Playful behaviors","Social robots"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social robotic donuts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83930460/Social_Robotic_Donuts_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381603","ids":["itu-15e5a132-c746-42ac-aa4f-38652d5db87c"],"keyword":["Air-actuated","Ambiguous form","Elastic expression","Playful behaviors","Social robots"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-4-5-F11E257D9A2B9C9ABF7F6E3D13270A16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83930460/Social_Robotic_Donuts_preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3309719","issn":["10725520","15583449"],"issn_org":["10725520"],"issue":"2","journal":"interactions","pages":"13","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"interactions","volume":"26"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-15e5a132-c746-42ac-aa4f-38652d5db87c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Social Robotic Donuts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381603","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The design of social robots usually does not focus on their kinetic expression, and often follows the assumption that their appearance should be human or animal like. To encourage a broader understanding of the possibilities for design of social robots, and as an inquiry into alternative relations with them, we present two robots, the Lat-Sac and the Blo-Nut, which are purposefully moving away from typical social robot design. We present how we engaged performance experts in the choreographic sketching of their elastic expression, and how we staged the robots in a fictitious near-future scenario to create a discursive space for reflection on emerging relations. Based on these encounters we discuss how acknowledging the otherness of social robots can be valuable in designing as well as growing intriguing relations with them.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Bewley, Harvey"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383146"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diegetic Prototype","Interactive Performance","Otherness","Research through Design","Social robots","Soft Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconfiguring the appearance and expression of social robots by acknowledging their otherness","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83256686/Reconfiguring_Social_Robots_camera_ready_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383146","identifier":[{"id":"85054040316","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-805ad222-ed0d-4f46-a166-83cd3f3a8f69"],"keyword":["Diegetic Prototype","Interactive Performance","Otherness","Research through Design","Social Robots","Soft Robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB27621B7A67053965A10F85F1DA2F34"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83256686/Reconfiguring_Social_Robots_camera_ready_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3196709.3196743","isbn":["9781450351980"],"pages":"667-677","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '18","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054040316"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-805ad222-ed0d-4f46-a166-83cd3f3a8f69"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reconfiguring the Appearance and Expression of Social Robots by Acknowledging their Otherness","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383146","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Both a provocative artistic object and research artefact, Blo-nut is part of a project where we explore novel robotic behaviour away from the mimicry of complex human expressions more commonly associated with robotic form and movement. In this pictorial we start by outlining our underlining design principles for the design process and use images to describe the making, real-time GUI and the \"choreographic sketching' of Blonut's movement characteristics. Finally, we argue for embracing novel and provoking 'otherness' in form and material when exploring interaction and communication with social robots.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bewley, Harvey","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384552"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreography","Expression","Non anthropomorphic","Otherness","Playfulness","Soft Robotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing blo nut design principles choreography and otherness in an expressive social robot","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83256665/paper163_pure_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384552","identifier":[{"id":"85054039256","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-df6b1199-f627-4f86-a226-67c66260b752"],"keyword":["Choreography","Expression","Non-anthropomorphic","Otherness","Playfulness","Soft Robotics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3EBEADFA3925D7CC2E33253B556E0CB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83256665/paper163_pure_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3196709.3196817","isbn":["9781450351980"],"pages":"1069-1080","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '18","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85054039256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-df6b1199-f627-4f86-a226-67c66260b752"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing Blo-nut: Design Principles, Choreography and Otherness in an Expressive Social Robot","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384552","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper offers four inspirational design patterns concerned with reducing inhibitions for unacquaintedco-located people to interact. These patterns identify impediments to interpersonal contact in relation to thedistances between people and present diverse examples of how these challenges may be addressed.Each inspirational design pattern offers strategies tomake social interaction more likely through enabling,encouraging or excusing people to move closertogether. The patterns are “Feel For Fun”, “ConjoiningSelf Images”, “Eye To Eye”, and “Nudge PeopleTogether”. Articulating possible approaches forincreasing conviviality may broaden the repertoire ofdevelopers concerned with social settings andcollaboration","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mitchell, Robb","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S02-086.21-038327"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2017-05-11","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"2017 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Collaboration","Design patterns","Social icebreaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"move closer towards design patterns to support initiating social encounters","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/140896234/Move_Closer_Towards_Design_Patterns_for_Initiating_Social_Encounters_CHI_ExtendedAbstract_Preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-086.21-038327","identifier":[{"id":"85019628863","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-752dcf32-b11b-46df-be99-f4cb56cec337","sdu-34950543-2e5b-4079-88d1-ef779d4c9d07"],"keyword":["Collaboration","Design patterns","Social icebreaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4D8BB3AAB51E55D3C3795255B1B6C111"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/140896234/Move_Closer_Towards_Design_Patterns_for_Initiating_Social_Encounters_CHI_ExtendedAbstract_Preprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010807/Move_Closer_small_cameraready.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication, SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Robb","key":"mitchellpau","last":"Mitchell","locid":"2e09e49e-5e3e-4a60-8766-df4bc3ad05db","name":"Mitchell, Robb","orcid":"0000-0002-8721-8330","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3027063.3053230","isbn":["9781450346566"],"pages":"2781-2787","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"CHI EA '17","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference Extended Abstracts on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019628863"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-752dcf32-b11b-46df-be99-f4cb56cec337","sdu-34950543-2e5b-4079-88d1-ef779d4c9d07"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Move Closer: Towards Design Patterns To Support Initiating Social Encounters","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.21-038327","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In the near future every other smart material will have computational power embedded in the form of graphene transistors or nanotubes. These will be the ultimate computational composites: materials that hold classic material qualities, such as structural durability, flexibility, texture, weight, and color, but additionally being capable of sensing, actuating, and computing. Indeed, computers will not be things in and by themselves, but embedded into the materials that make up our surroundings. This also means that the way we interact with computers and the way we program them, will change. Consequently we ask what the practice of programming and giving form to such materials would be like? How would we be able to familiarize ourselves with the dynamics of these materials and their different combinations of cause and effect? Which tools would we need and what would they look like? Will we program these computational composites through external computers and then transfer the code them, or will the programming happen closer to the materials? In this feature we outline a new research program that floats between imagined futures and the development of a material programming practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384784"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Graphene Transistors","Material Programming Practice","Nanotubes","Smart materials"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82382888/MATERIAL_PROGRAMMING.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384784","identifier":[{"id":"85018939771","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-eeb6cd45-99ad-4dad-b873-f5e373bcc7c7"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Graphene Transistors","Material Programming Practice","Nanotubes","Smart Materials"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6126F664DE2ECDDE18FE69FB0914F9D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82382888/MATERIAL_PROGRAMMING.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3057277","issn":["10725520","15583449"],"issn_org":["10725520"],"issue":"3","journal":"interactions","pages":"36-41","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"interactions","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018939771"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eeb6cd45-99ad-4dad-b873-f5e373bcc7c7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Material Programming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384784","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this pictorial we present the form-giving process of a Hedonic Haptic player, a wearable device that plays vibrotactile patterns on the body. We depict how we explored the aesthetics of the vibrotactile design space, how we constructed a platform as body of a hedonic experience, and how we developed different vibrotactile compositions. These activities collectively show how combinations of experiencing form, composing form, and materializing form can contribute to the aesthetic form-giving practice in interaction design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Vallgårda, Anna","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384814"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic interfaces","Pleasure","Vibrotactile"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"giving form to a hedonic haptics player","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010769/PictorialDIS2017_Final_V2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384814","identifier":[{"id":"85022215742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f12e922f-0156-415a-a03e-e603b2555656"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic Interfaces","Pleasure","Vibrotactile"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16FC5BC1ACDA106C10DEDD022387EACC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010769/PictorialDIS2017_Final_V2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064663.3064792","isbn":["9781450349222"],"pages":"903-914","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 Conference on Designing Interactive Systems","title":"DIS '17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022215742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f12e922f-0156-415a-a03e-e603b2555656"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Giving Form to a Hedonic Haptics Player","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384814","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this design case we present the Hedonic Haptic Player—a wearable device that plays different patterns of vibrations on the body as a form of music for the skin. With this we begin to explore the enjoyability of vibrations in a wearable set-up. Instead of implementing vibrations as a haptic output for some form of communication we want to explore their hedonistic value. The process leading up to the Hedonic Haptic player served as a first step in getting a grasp of the design space of vibrotactile stimuli in a broader sense. This is reported as seven episodes of explorations. The Hedonic Haptic player is currently equipped with three compositions, including an ambient, a rhythmic, and a combination of the two. We explore the value of the experiences they afford through two types of design critique, one from external experts and one auto-critique. We conclude that the vibrotactile stimuli we have created seems to be an acquired taste but that they can indeed create some novel and enjoyable experiences.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382131"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Pleasure","Vibrotactile","haptic design","hedonic design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hedonic haptic player","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442931/2860_10256_4_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382131","identifier":[{"id":"85040075474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3af7d376-6ff6-4174-84bc-38034822a3d9"],"keyword":["Pleasure","Vibrotactile","haptic design","hedonic design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-AE5317EBB5C7AD0AEB982BC71B1926D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442931/2860_10256_4_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ijdesign.org/index.php/IJDesign/article/view/2860/789","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19913761","1994036X"],"issn_org":["19913761"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Design","pages":"17-33","publisher":"National Taiwan University of Science and Technology","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Design","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040075474"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3af7d376-6ff6-4174-84bc-38034822a3d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Hedonic Haptic Player","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382131","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The Hedonic Haptics player is a portable wearable device that plays back vibrotactile compositions. It consists of three domes each of which houses a vibration motor providing vibrotactile sensations to the wearer. The domes are connected to a control unit the size of a small Walkman. The Hedonic Haptics player can store up to ten different compositions made up of haptic signals varying in amplitude, waveform and length. We use these different compositions to explore the aesthetic potential of vibrational haptics in an embodied wearable setup.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Vallgårda, Anna","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383482"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic interfaces","Vibrotactile stimuli","Wearable technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hedonic haptics player a wearable device to experience vibrotactile compositions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010785/Demo_DIS_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383482","identifier":[{"id":"85022220970","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-96c80086-9971-487f-a1ce-9420cb544068"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic Interfaces","Vibrotactile stimuli","Wearable Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0762AF97378241F6D28023F76E208E75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010785/Demo_DIS_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064857.3079178","isbn":["9781450349918"],"pages":"297-300","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems","title":"DIS '17 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022220970"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-96c80086-9971-487f-a1ce-9420cb544068"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Hedonic Haptics Player: A Wearable Device to Experience Vibrotactile Compositions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383482","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We propose the notion of material programming as a new practice for designing future interactive artifacts. Material programming would be a way for the interaction designer to better explore the dynamics of the materials at hand and through that familiarity be able to compose more sophisticated and complex temporal forms in their designs. As such it would blur the boundaries between programming and crafting these new smart and computational materials. We envision a material programming practice developed around physical tools (e.g. Fig 1) that draw on bodily skills and experiences (Fig 2) while enabling actions performed directly on the material with immediate effects (no program vs. execution mode). Finally, the tools would enable one layer of abstraction and as such encompass the potential of the computational materials but not that of possibly adjacent computers, which could run more complex algorithms.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381637"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart materials","Temporal Forms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming a new interaction design practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84978650812","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381637","identifier":[{"id":"84978650812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-18c8171c-0bc6-4b54-833d-3bd2c500c498"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart Materials","Temporal Forms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE23E7CF55E7C28ED96546A2DC5E128C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908805.2909411","eisbn":["9781450343152"],"pages":"149-152","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '16 Companion","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978650812"],"search":{"DAF":["All