{"abstract":"Participatory processes of innovation occur in moments of conflict and reconciliation across stakeholders’ voices. As such, participating in these processes presumes that stakeholders have an awareness of the products and identity of the ‘stakes’ they represent – and that they are able to articulate these. In this paper I present how critical artefacts can be directed at stakeholders from industry, as a tool to support and provoke articulated reflections on organizational identity and products. Based on experiences from a project that brought together five industrial organizations that all delivered indoor climate related products or services, I propose that critical artefacts benefit articulated introspections on organizational products and identity when these artefacts are technically feasible yet not in accordance to core company principles or norms.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038300"],"event":{"acronym":"PIN-C","end":"2013-06-20","place":"Lahti, fi","start":"2013-06-18","title":"3rd Participatory Innovation Conference","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Critical Artefacts","Critical design","Industrial Reflection","Organizational identity","Participatory Innovation","Stakeholder Awareness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"giving critical form to organizational vision as tool for introspection","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lut.fi/documents/27578/292022/PIN-C+2013_Proceedings_HQ.pdf/17fa385b-cc30-4ae4-82a6-59308a80d503","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038300","ids":["itu-535b99bc-ffc5-4fa5-9b66-fdd997532940","sdu-c04b9d40-62ec-4b58-a622-49a9215bca94"],"keyword":["Critical Artefacts","Critical Design","Industrial Reflection","Organizational Identity","Participatory Innovation","Stakeholder Awareness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-5A3B22F5EC65089FBCD4A1CA365C6E11"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lut.fi/documents/27578/292022/PIN-C+2013_Proceedings_HQ.pdf/17fa385b-cc30-4ae4-82a6-59308a80d503","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helinä","key":"melkaspedh","last":"Melkas","name":"Melkas, Helinä","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"buurpedh","last":"Buur","name":"Buur, Jacob","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9789522653925"],"isbn":["9789522653918"],"issn":["22433376"],"issue":"6","pages":"68-75","publisher":"Lappeenranta University of Technology","series":"LUT Scientific and Expertise Publications. Tutkimusraportit - Research Reports","status":"p","subtitle":"PIN-C 2013","title":"Proceedings of the Participatory Innovation Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-535b99bc-ffc5-4fa5-9b66-fdd997532940","sdu-c04b9d40-62ec-4b58-a622-49a9215bca94"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Giving critical form to organizational vision as tool for introspection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038300","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Design researchers have an important role to play when engaged with user-driven design projects in industry. Design researchers can craft ethnographic material to facilitate transfers of user-knowledge to industry, and demonstrate how this material can be used in the design of new products and services. However, ethnographic findings can reveal issues that are at tension with conceptions of the project members from industry. Other than brushing these tensions aside, we propose provotyping (provocative prototyping) as an approach to constructively build on them as a resource for change. Provotypes are ethnographically rooted, technically working, robust artefacts that deliberately challenge stakeholder conceptions by reifying and exposing tensions that surround a field of organizational interest. The daily and local experience of provotypes aim to stir dialectical processes of reflection on how conceptions currently are, and fuel the front end of a development process by speculating how conceptions could be different. In this article we start by making explicit the relation between provotypes, practices of critical design and organizational sense-making. We then illustrate through a multi-stakeholder project that concerned the field of indoor climate how provotypes facilitate transfers of user knowledge to industry, and how they contribute to the development of new products and services. We end by framing the role of the design researcher and discuss the politics that are inherent to design provocations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Donovan, Jared","Buur, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-099.38-038325"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queensland University of Technology"],"keyword":["Critical design","Participatory Innovation","Provotyping","organisationalsense making"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenging industry conceptions with provotypes","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15710882.2013.788193","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.38-038325","identifier":[{"id":"84878665761","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7474139e-f7ab-4ce7-a201-80925c1c6093","sdu-8405458d-5f66-4564-be1b-79583edf9b74"],"keyword":["critical design","organisationalsense-making","organizational sense-making","participatory innovation","provotyping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8518BD5D18022E5E8005FBC9B936B3F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/15710882.2013.788193","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"queensland university of technology","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Queensland University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jared","key":"donovanpau","last":"Donovan","name":"Donovan, Jared","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"buurpau","last":"Buur","locid":"c6a97ac7-3313-470b-b896-9958e843f962","name":"Buur, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-3320-1031","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/15710882.2013.788193","issn":["15710882","17453755"],"issn_org":["15710882"],"issue":"2","journal":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","pages":"73-89","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"CoDesign: International Journal of CoCreation in Design and the Arts","title_org":"CoDesign","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878665761"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7474139e-f7ab-4ce7-a201-80925c1c6093","sdu-8405458d-5f66-4564-be1b-79583edf9b74"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Challenging industry conceptions with provotypes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.38-038325","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Double paper to be presented together with Laurens Boer, Mads Clausen Institute, Spire, University of Southern Denmark.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Mie Femø","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-508372"],"event":{"end":"2013-06-20","place":"Lahti, fi","start":"2013-06-18","title":"Participatory Innovation Conference","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of organizational vision and values in creative design processes aesthetics of designed participation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lut.fi/c/document_library/get_file?groupId=27578&uuid=95368521-ec20-4896-87b4-b779956d0da8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-508372","ids":["ku-c09b317d-0f28-41a9-b0d6-8980b6d510b7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FC82D9433E796C14B360BB958491C474"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.lut.fi/c/document_library/get_file?groupId=27578&uuid=95368521-ec20-4896-87b4-b779956d0da8","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mie Femø","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b704cee2-057e-4bdb-9565-a1ef4e06506e","name":"Nielsen, Mie Femø","orcid":"0000-0003-2418-1590","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","name":"Boer, Laurens","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c09b317d-0f28-41a9-b0d6-8980b6d510b7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Role of Organizational Vision and Values in Creative Design Processes : Aesthetics of designed participation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-508372","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Central to multi-stakeholder processes of participatory innovation is to generate knowledge about ‘users’ and to identify business opportunities accordingly. In these processes of collaborative analysis and synthesis, conflicting perceptions within and about a field of interest are likely to surface. Instead of the natural tendency to avoid these tensions, we demonstrate how tensions can be utilized by embodying them in provocative types (provotypes). Provotypes expose and embody tensions that surround a field of interest to support collaborative analysis and collaborative design explorations across stakeholders. In this paper we map how provotyping contributes to four related areas of contemporary Interaction Design practice. Through a case study that brings together stakeholders from the field of indoor climate, we provide characteristics of design provocations and design guidelines for provotypes for participatory innovation.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Donovan, Jared"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038410"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queensland University of Technology"],"keyword":["Collaborative design","Critical design","Interaction Design Practice","Multi Stakeholder Processes","Participatory Innovation","Provotypes","Provotyping","User Centered Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"provotypes for participatory innovation","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-038410","identifier":[{"id":"84864764778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f2dd4330-5f3b-4487-a7b1-3dcd4c8450be","sdu-5ddbb7ff-5012-4d75-bfe6-403a33bc8e5b"],"keyword":["Collaborative Design","Critical Design","Interaction Design Practice","Multi-Stakeholder Processes","Participatory innovation","Provotypes","Provotyping","User-centered design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-2092B386F57AEC6D005088729AF7624B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"queensland university of technology","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Queensland University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jared","key":"donovanpau","last":"Donovan","name":"Donovan, Jared","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f2dd4330-5f3b-4487-a7b1-3dcd4c8450be","sdu-5ddbb7ff-5012-4d75-bfe6-403a33bc8e5b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Provotypes for Participatory Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038410","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In the context of industrial innovation projects, ethnographic research is often employed to inform and inspire the development of a new product or service which fits the intended use context. However, user conceptions that are revealed through ethnographic research are often at odds with developers’ taken-for-granted conceptions about this use context. Design proposals resulting from such projects typically not only embed the ethnographic findings, but also these taken-for-granted conceptions. On the one hand, this can be problematic at the end of the development process (e.g. when a product is put on the market and mismatches use context), but on the other hand, it creates an opportunity for reflection on these conceptions when revealed at the front end of innovation projects. Design researchers can play an important role in bringing conceptual tensions between stakeholders to the foreground, by demonstrating what these tensions might mean in light of new product or service development. In this dissertation, I rekindle the provotyping approach from the 1990’s systems design community, as this approach argued to expose discrepancies in practice in order to devise qualitatively new systems. Based on my participation in a project that involved industries in the field of indoor climate, and that employed ethnographic research to inform and inspire the development of new products or services, I develop the approach with respect to contemporary design research concerns, notably the research areas of critical design and participatory innovation. I propose provotypes as ethnographically rooted, technically working, robust artefacts that deliberately challenge stakeholder conceptions by reifying tensions that surround a use context of organizational interest. I show how provotypes can be brought into use and developers’ context. Provotypes can be brought into the previously studied use context to conduct generative design research, which inspires and informs the design process with user knowledge about the reified tension. Provotypes can also be brought into the industrial context, to provoke project partners from industry to experience on a local and daily basis how industrial taken-for-granted conceptions can become problematic in the development of new products or services. It is beneficial to reveal conceptual tensions early in the development process as it leaves room to implement reframed conceptions in subsequent prototyping and concept development activities. The design qualities that provotypes entail provide handles for the design researcher and stakeholders to collaboratively explore new product or service directions, as these design qualities relate to use context. Provotypes therefore can synthesise analytical and generative activities in innovation projects. Overall, this dissertation argues that design researchers can approach early stages of an innovation project as opportunities to tease out conceptual tensions between use context and industrial context. I provide design guidelines and design characteristics of provotypes to support design researchers in developing provotypes. This dissertation can as such support design researchers in the transfer of user-knowledge that is at odds with industry conceptions, and in cautiously bringing ethnographic and design endeavours together.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671914"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Critical design","Generative Design Research","New product development","Participatory Innovation","Provotypes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how provotypes challenge stakeholder conceptions in innovation projects","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-671914","ids":["sdu-e006832d-edbd-44a7-95d8-36919b494fed"],"keyword":["Critical Design","Generative Design Research","New Product Development","Participatory innovation","Provotypes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-59E1C28C8FEC71B3E11210F2D89756D1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"160","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet. Det Tekniske Fakultet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e006832d-edbd-44a7-95d8-36919b494fed"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How Provotypes Challenge Stakeholder Conceptions in Innovation Projects","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671914","year":"2012","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In this paper I revisit the provotyping approach and apply it in a participatory innovation setting. Through a case study within the field of indoor climate I describe the implications for the approach when it becomes part of a participatory innovation process, next to the opportunities it creates.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Case study","Indoor climate","Innovation process","Participatory Innovation","Provotyping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"participatory provocation","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-038259","ids":["itu-15d32e1b-b47b-4399-91dd-7364e6efcd62","sdu-12053822-ffb4-4b91-96a3-21b6dc131f5c"],"keyword":["Participatory Innovation","Provotyping Approach","case study","indoor climate","innovation process","provotyping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-B3E3A45A82EDC77C644079CB7151AB40"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"21-26","place":"Sønderborg","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 1st Participatory Innovation Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-15d32e1b-b47b-4399-91dd-7364e6efcd62","sdu-12053822-ffb4-4b91-96a3-21b6dc131f5c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Participatory Provocation?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038259","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we describe how ongoing work with ethnographic material in a participatory innovation sets the scene for innovation to happen. We elaborate on how actionable formats of ethnographic material have been mediated to industrial partners with a stake in an innovation project. We illustrate how the stakeholders engaged in activities such as sense-making, co-analysis, and cross-comparison of the ethnographic materials, and the specification and mapping of innovation opportunities. We argue that these activities served to establish a shared understanding and ownership of the participatory research, design material.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jaffari, Svenja Désirée","Boer, Laurens","Buur, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-091.89-038388"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-22","place":"Orlando (Florida), us","start":"2011-07-19","title":"The 15th World Multi-conference on Systemics, Cybernetics and Informatics","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Co Analysis","Design methods","Ethnographic Material","Ethnography","Participatory Innovation","Sense making","Stakeholder engagement","Stakeholder involvement","Workshop Facilitation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"actionable ethnography in participatory innovation a case study","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84867519031","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-091.89-038388","identifier":[{"id":"84867519031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d58b1fab-41a3-4e78-bb32-4c272021a1f9","sdu-2e1b155a-a5ca-47eb-b4a6-d8769d999887"],"keyword":["Co-Analysis","Design Methods","Ethnographic Material","Ethnography","Participatory Innovation","Sense-Making","Stakeholder Engagement","Stakeholder Involvement","Workshop Facilitation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-14C6686BC4BD574C8E14DF74775A351B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svenja","key":"jaffaripau","last":"Jaffari","locid":"fa25a1a1-03c6-4f73-a9c1-a94736985e65","name":"Jaffari, Svenja Désirée","name_org":"Jaffari, Svenja","orcid":"0009-0000-7544-3250","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"buurpau","last":"Buur","locid":"c6a97ac7-3313-470b-b896-9958e843f962","name":"Buur, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-3320-1031","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"100-106","place":"Orlando (Florida)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of The 15th World Multi-conference on Systemics, Cybernetics and Informatics","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d58b1fab-41a3-4e78-bb32-4c272021a1f9","sdu-2e1b155a-a5ca-47eb-b4a6-d8769d999887"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Actionable Ethnography in Participatory Innovation: A Case Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.89-038388","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we describe an opportunity that Ambient Intelligence provides outside the domains typically associated with it. We present a concept for enhancing child development by introducing tangible computing in a way that fits the children and improves current education. We argue that the interfaces used should be simple and make sense to the children. The computer should be hidden and interaction should take place through familiar play objects to which the children already have a connection. Contrary to a straightforward application of personal computers, our solution addresses cognitive, social and fine motor skills in an integrated manner. We illustrate our vision with a concrete example of an application that supports the inevitable transition from free play throughout the classroom to focused play at the desk. We also present the validation of the concept with children, parents and teachers, highlighting that they all recognize the benefits of tangible computing in this domain.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Verhaegh, J.","Fontijn, W.","Aarts, E.","Boer, Laurens","van de Wouw, D."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-038256"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Ambient intelligence","Child Development","Validation","tangible interfaces"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a development support bubble for children","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/ais-2011-0092","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-038256","identifier":[{"id":"79251513323","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-11108724-bd5f-4e66-878b-08f5c649f9b8","sdu-3b56ec75-225c-4696-a306-8fda9ee77391"],"keyword":["Ambient Intelligence","child development","tangible interfaces","validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4D4DE8977BFCCBD11D65F7D6D47E04F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/ais-2011-0092","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI), SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"verhaeghpau","last":"Verhaegh","name":"Verhaegh, J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"W.","key":"fontijnpau","last":"Fontijn","name":"Fontijn, W.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"E.","key":"aartspau","last":"Aarts","name":"Aarts, E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","name_org":"Boer, L.","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"vandewouwpau","last":"van de Wouw","name":"van de Wouw, D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/ais-2011-0092","issn":["18761364"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Ambient Intelligence and Smart Environments","pages":"27-35","publisher":"IOS Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Ambient Intelligence and Smart Environments","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79251513323"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-11108724-bd5f-4e66-878b-08f5c649f9b8","sdu-3b56ec75-225c-4696-a306-8fda9ee77391"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A development support bubble for children","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038256","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The key element in participatory innovation is to understand innovation as a social problem solving process between different stakeholders. The social dynamics amongst stakeholders are fundamental to the participatory process and outcome, and it’s therefore beneficial for facilitators and stakeholders themselves to understand their relations and what it means to participate. We argue that we can grasp these social dynamics of participatory innovation through play. From a management perspective we study how playing games helps us to understand these dynamics, while from an interaction design perspective we study how a game that addresses these dynamics can be designed. We describe a case of a game, designed for the Participatory Innovation Conference of 2011 in Sønderborg, Denmark. The game was particularly designed around the themes of conflict and interdependence, captured by the dilemma of co-opetition where individual and group goals are conflicting. Drawing on observations and video data of the game being played by the participants of the conference, we study how different group compositions deal with novelty. From here we explain how the process of play can help to grasp the social dynamics of participatory innovation, and outline design strategies to do this.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sproedt, Henrik","Boer, Laurens"],"cuid":["S02-092.68-038405"],"event":{"acronym":"CINet Conference","end":"2011-09-13","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2011-09-11","title":"12th International CINet Conference","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Game based learning","Innovation management","Interaction design","Participatory Innovation","Social dynamics","Stakeholder Interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"grasping social dynamics of participatory innovation a case of playing a game","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-092.68-038405","ids":["itu-e91545c9-aea2-4c34-9013-6dede548bf39","sdu-e75a5e14-17d6-45c0-b6d4-54f427348d94"],"keyword":["Game-Based Learning","Innovation Management","Interaction Design","Participatory Innovation","Social Dynamics","Stakeholder Interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-83F5F0EAB9CF78345080E359D73C2BB5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Technology Entrepreneurship and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"sproedtpau","last":"Sproedt","locid":"1dffc0cb-d58e-4145-94b2-9a0b950b3070","name":"Sproedt, Henrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"fc836b75-73f9-4f9d-b648-cdf97b9edae3","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789077360002"],"status":"p","subtitle":"Continuous Innovation: Doing More with Less","title":"Proceedings 12th CINet conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e91545c9-aea2-4c34-9013-6dede548bf39","sdu-e75a5e14-17d6-45c0-b6d4-54f427348d94"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Grasping social dynamics of participatory innovation : A case of playing a game","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.68-038405","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
